ore relaxed, but there is still that fun nightlife vibe on a Saturday night where you see various street performers and quaint local bars that cater to a diverse demographic. I also found that the bathrooms in these bars were a lot cleaner and the street overall had a better smell than Bourbon. Bourbon Street is not at all a bad place to go, but it is primarily what your individual tastes are; these two ..."},{"business_id":"OZ0WENoroBhh-D9CAjDwrg","review_id":"8xCx9yjDF4E1VpPBI3mU0w","date":"2017-10-17T19:10:57","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9117199778556824,"text_excerpt":"The most delicious drinks (wine, beer, and hand crafted cocktails!) + Fresh Seafood (crab cakes anyone?) + TONS of restaurants, bars and jazz clubs + Killer live music - inside and out! + Crowds galore - but all down for a good time! + All the best vibes ________________________________ Frenchman Street in a nutshell! I LOVED IT AND YOU WILL TOO! :)"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
